@HostAddress = http://localhost:5142

### 1. Create a Valid High-Priority Notification
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-101",
  "type": "Email",
  "recipient": "customer@example.com",
  "subject": "Order Confirmed",
  "message": "Your order #1001 has been confirmed and is being packed.",
  "priority": "High",
  "requestedDeliveryTime": "2026-10-29T12:30:00Z"
}

###

### 2. Test Idempotency / Duplicate Prevention (Send twice within 5 mins)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ORDER-1001-CONFIRMATION

{
  "customerId": "CUST-101",
  "type": "Email",
  "recipient": "customer@example.com",
  "subject": "Order Confirmed",
  "message": "Your order #1001 has been confirmed and is being packed.",
  "priority": "High",
  "requestedDeliveryTime": "2026-10-29T12:30:00Z"
}

###

### 3. Test Validation Failure (Invalid email, missing message, past delivery time)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "",
  "type": "SMS",
  "recipient": "invalid-email-format",
  "priority": "Urgent",
  "requestedDeliveryTime": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 4. Test Simulated Provider Failure (Recipient starting with 'fail@')
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-999",
  "type": "Email",
  "recipient": "fail@example.com",
  "subject": "Simulated Gateway Failure",
  "message": "This notification tests resilient error handling without crashing.",
  "priority": "Normal"
}

###

### 5. Trigger Processing for All Eligible Pending Notifications
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications/process

###

### 6. Get Notifications for a Customer
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications/customer/CUST-101
Accept: application/json

###

### 7. Get All Notifications (with optional filters)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications
Accept: application/json

###

### 8. Get Notification by ID (Replace with an existing GUID)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json

###

### 9. Filter Notifications by Status (Sent, Pending, Failed)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications?status=Sent
Accept: application/json

###

### 10. Filter Notifications by Customer ID and Status
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications?customerId=CUST-101&status=Pending
Accept: application/json

###

### 11. Trigger Processing for a Single Notification by ID (Replace with a Pending GUID)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/notifications/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/process
Accept: application/json

